Survive a NIC that goes away and comes back

A USB adapter that was unplugged or reset by USB has no IPv4 address for a
few seconds after it returns. Inferno panicked in Settings (BIND_IP has no
IPv4), which inside PipeWire aborts the whole process: PipeWire crash-looped
until systemd gave up. Wait up to 10 s for the address instead.

While the NIC was gone, a failed send left next_ts unchanged, so the TX
thread retried the same packet in a catch-up loop and logged thousands of
errors per second. Skip the packet and log at most once a second.

